nverting peak-to-peak to amplitude gives Vmax = 4 V and Vmin = 2 V, which is also correct.\",\n      \"The waveform assignments are correct. v1 is the transformer-coupled high-frequency carrier, (c). v2 is the low-frequency signal wave in series with bias supply E1, (a). v3 is the tuned-tank output, the AM wave (b). The circuit applies the signal wave to the base, so (ア) is ベース and this is a base modulation circuit.\",\n      \"Option-by-option errors checked. (1) Only (ア) is wrong. (2) (ア) is wrong, (ウ) and (エ) are swapped, and 8/12 ≈ 67%. (3) (イ) and (エ) are swapped, and (8 − 4)/8 = 50%. (4) (ア) is wrong, and all three of v1, v2 and v3 differ from the correct assignment (b≠c, c≠a, a≠b). Each option's explanation matches these errors and is consistent with the arithmetic.\",\n      \"The published candidate figure is a crop of the official page 22 containing Figure 1 and Figure 2(a)–(c). It includes every label: v1, v2, v3, E1, E2, the arrows, 8 V, 4 V, '破線は包絡線を示す', and both captions. The candidate figure alone is enough to understand and answer the question.\",\n      \"Source URLs: the question file q01 and the answer file a01 match the 2024-08-18 session. reviewedFromPage [24, 25] matches the T1-R 024/025 markers on the original pages. There are no officialReferenceUrls, so no separate primary source needed checking.\"\n    ]\n  }\n]\n```"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":22968,"cache_read_input_tokens":140085,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":22968},"output_tokens":7,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"2ddbbad0-5451-4b66-bbd1-ab1b4194b393","uuid":"7add1419-c547-4431-a1e4-6c86171f67c3","timestamp":"2026-09-24T05:27:42.513Z","request_id":"req_011CfMiA6HxxzwCGwXbzaiPK"}
